\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Two counterpropagating light beams enter the fiber loop at the \textit  {Entry point}. Their phase is initially in sync. After the transit time $\tau $ they exit and interfere. However, during that time, the \textit  {Entry/Exit point} has moved according to rotation rate $\omega $ (by the angle $\alpha = \omega \cdot \tau $) and the CW and CCW beams covered non--equal path lengths ($L\pm \Delta {}l$). In result they differ in phase. }}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
